    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d301">

                <pb facs="0327" n="303" sameAs="frus:frus1864p4/pg303"/>

                <head ana="#head_untitled-missing-head-in-printed-volume">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">United States Consulate</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#small-caps">Azores</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Fayal</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1864-04-29"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 29,
                        1864</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have just received information (which I
                    hasten to communicate to you) that the English double-screw steamer Atalanta,
                    ostensibly <hi rendition="#italic">four</hi> days from Falmouth, bound to
                    Bermuda, in ballast, was at Terceira for coals, on the 11th instant. She is said
                    to have run across from Calais to Dover in seventy-five minutes.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, respectfully, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>CHARLES W. DABNEY.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">James E. Harvey</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">United States Minister Resident, Lisbon.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
